<%#
  Involuntary-downgrade grace banner (projects.md §6/§7/§12-J). Shown while the
  account owes a choose-N decision after a card failure / cancel dropped it to Free
  over the cap. The point: NOTHING was suspended — every monitor keeps running —
  but the user must pick which FREE_PLAN_MONITOR_LIMIT to keep by the deadline, or
  the daily backstop keeps the oldest N for them. Only rendered when billing is
  enabled and current_user.must_choose_downgrade? (the layout gates both).

  The lock itself is only released on a billing page load, so an account can sit
  here having already put itself back within the cap — by deleting monitors, or by
  a voluntary downgrade that raced its own cancel webhook (M4/M3). There is nothing
  to choose in that state, so the banner says so and points at Billing, which
  releases the lock on load. Counts are of monitors occupying a cap slot: suspended
  ones don't count anywhere else either (locked decision #8).
%>
<% deadline = current_user.downgrade_choice_deadline_at %>
<% limit = Stablemate::FREE_PLAN_MONITOR_LIMIT %>
<% active_count = current_user.monitors.counting_toward_cap.count %>
<div class="mb-6 rounded-xl border border-pending-dot bg-pending-bg px-5 py-4 shadow-sm"
     role="alert" data-testid="downgrade-grace-banner">
  <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
    <% if active_count > limit %>
      <div>
        <p class="text-[14px] font-semibold text-pending-text">
          Your plan dropped to Free — choose which monitors to keep
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-[13px] text-pending-text/90">
          You have <strong><%= pluralize(active_count, "monitor") %></strong>,
          but Free covers <%= limit %>. Nothing was suspended —
          all of them are still running. Pick the <%= limit %> to keep active
          <% if deadline %>by <strong><%= deadline.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %></strong><% end %>,
          or we'll keep your oldest <%= limit %> for you.
        </p>
      </div>
      <%= link_to "Choose monitors", new_billing_downgrade_path,
            class: "shrink-0 inline-flex items-center h-9 px-4 rounded-lg bg-brand text-white text-[13px] font-semibold hover:bg-brand-hover whitespace-nowrap",
            data: { testid: "grace-choose-link" } %>
    <% else %>
      <div>
        <p class="text-[14px] font-semibold text-pending-text">
          Your plan dropped to Free
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-[13px] text-pending-text/90">
          Your <strong><%= pluralize(active_count, "monitor") %></strong>
          fit within the Free plan's <%= limit %>, so nothing will be suspended and
          there's nothing to choose.
        </p>
      </div>
      <%= link_to "Review billing", billing_subscription_path,
            class: "shrink-0 inline-flex items-center h-9 px-4 rounded-lg bg-brand text-white text-[13px] font-semibold hover:bg-brand-hover whitespace-nowrap",
            data: { testid: "grace-review-link" } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
